.TH LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK 3 LIBRECRYPT
.SH NAME
LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK - Compare version against linked against version

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <librecrypt.h>

extern const int \fBlibrecrypt_version_major\fP;
extern const int \fBlibrecrypt_version_minor\fP;
extern const int \fBlibrecrypt_version_patch\fP;

#define \fBLIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK\fP(\fIMAJOR\fP, \fIMINOR\fP, \fIPATCH\fP) /* implementation omitted */

.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lrecrypt .

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR librecrypt_version_major ,
.BR librecrypt_version_minor ,
and
.B librecrypt_version_patch
variables describe the version number of the
version of
.B librecrypt
that the application is linked against.
.PP
.B librecrypt_version_major
is the major number. It is increased when there
are backwards incompatible changes, necessitating
the that the application is recompiled or even
rewritten
.PP
.B librecrypt_version_minor
is the minor number. It is increased when the API
is extended. It is reset to zero when the major
number is modified.
.PP
.B librecrypt_version_patch
is the patch number. It is increased when the
software is modified but the API and ABI are
unmodified. It is reset to zero when the major or
minor number is modified.
.PP
The
.B LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK
macro compares
.IR MAJOR ,
.IR MINOR ,
and
.I PATCH
against
.BR librecrypt_version_major ,
.BR librecrypt_version_minor ,
and
.BR librecrypt_version_patch .
.PP
If the versions are the same, the macro expands to an
expression with the value 0 and the type
.IR int .
.PP
If the specified version is newer than the version
the application is linked against, the macro expands
to an expression with a positive value of the type
.IR int .
.PP
If the specified version is older than the version
the application is linked against, the macro expands
to an expression with a negative value of the type
.IR int .
.PP
If the versions are different, the most most significant
different number determines the absolute value of the
value the macro expands to. If the major numbers are
different, the absolute value is 3, otherwise if the
minor numbers are different, the absolute value is 3,
otherwise (if the patch numbers are different), the
absolute value is 1.

.SH APPLICATION USAGE
Because these variables were introduced in version
1.2 of
.BR librecrypt ,
it is impossible to check the exact version if
it is lower than 1.2, however, using weak
linkage it is possible to check if the linked
version is lower than 1.2: in your application
define this variable with weak linkage. You
can set it to 0 and let the library replace it
if it has defined it, or you can simply declare
it as an external symbol without providing it:
then taking the address of it will return
.B NULL
if it doesn't exist: you can use this trick with
any function may be want to use as well.
.PP
Additionally, without
.BR librecrypt_version_major ,
.BR librecrypt_version_minor ,
and
.B librecrypt_version_patch
properly linked,
.B LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK
will fail at runtime.

.SH NOTES
The version number of
.B librecrypt
is formatted as
.IR major.minor.patch.revision ,
or
.IR major.minor.patch
when
.I reversion
is 0, or
.IR major.minor
when both
.I patch
and
.I revision
are 0.
.PP
.I revision
cannot be tested agaist since it is only incremented
when no changes are made to the library software but
for example only to documentation or build script
(or reset to 0 when any of the other numbers are modified).

.SH HISTORY
The
.BR librecrypt_version_major ,
.BR librecrypt_version_minor ,
and
.B librecrypt_version_patch
variables and the
.B LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_LINK
macro were introduced in version 1.2 of
.BR librecrypt .

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librecrypt (7),
.BR LIBRECRYPT_VERSION_CMP_BUILD (3)
